-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  suite_cli_help.adam - `adam help`: the banner, then adam's own help, every
  list and column from the CLI's command and option tables (an option that
  belongs to some commands only names them), exit 0
*******************************************************************************/

/*
@@test
  kind cli
  targets x86_64-windows-gnu
  args "help"
  exitcode 0
  | Adam™ CLI v0.1.0
  | Copyright © 2026-present tinyBigGAMES™ LLC, All Rights Reserved.
  | https://adamlang.org
  |
  | USAGE:
  |   adam <command> [options]
  |
  | COMMANDS:
  |   build   [<file|folder>]       Build the program whose main module is <file>, or the project whose project.toml is in <folder> (default: the current folder), into an exe
  |   check   <file>                Check the program whose main module is <file>: the front end only, nothing built
  |   init    <name> <exe|dll|lib>  Make a new project in the folder <name> under the current folder: project.toml, src/<name>.adam and assets/
  |   pack    [<folder>]            Zip the assets folder of the project whose project.toml is in <folder> (default: the current folder) into <name>.rez in its output folder, with its pack password; every build copies it beside its exe
  |   info    [<folder>]            Print the project whose project.toml is in <folder> (default: the current folder) as one line of JSON, for an editor
  |   cimport <spec>                Turn the C headers an import spec (<name>.cimport.toml) names into an Adam .C binding unit
  |   dap                           Serve the Debug Adapter Protocol on stdin / stdout, for an editor's debugger
  |   lsp                           Serve the Language Server Protocol on stdin / stdout, for an editor's diagnostics
  |   editor  [<file> ...]          Start the Adam editor on its own, with each <file> open; adam returns at once
  |   help    [<command>]           Show this help, or one command's
  |
  | OPTIONS:
  |   -o, --output     <dir>        The output folder: build writes the exe to its bin (else the main module's @outputpath, else its project's output folder, else output under the working folder); cimport writes the unit into it (else the spec's output folder, else the spec's own) (build, cimport only)
  |   -t, --target     <triple>     The target, by its triple (TARGETS lists them); wins over the main module's @target (build, check, cimport only)
  |   -opt, --optimize <level>      The optimization level: debug, safe, fast or small; wins over the main module's @optimize (build, check only)
  |   --defaults                    -t / -opt only stand in where the main module has no @target / @optimize (an editor's toolbar) (build, check only)
  |   -r, --run                     Run the exe once built, in its folder (an x86_64-linux-gnu one through WSL); the arguments after -- are its own (build only)
  |   -d, --debug                   Debug the exe once built, in this console (h lists the debugger's commands); the arguments after -- are its own (build only)
  |   --host           <exe>        With -d on a dll: the exe that loads it, run and debugged with the dll's lines (build only)
  |   --emit-ir                     Also write <name>.ir beside the exe: the optimized IR of the program's own units, with each function's analysis (build only)
  |   --emit-pp                     Print the headers as preprocessed (clang -E's text: line markers, then the tokens) and stop there (cimport only)
  |   --emit-unit                   Also print the Adam unit the import wrote (cimport only)
  |   --emit-layout                 Also print the unit's layout probe: C _Static_asserts of every record as Adam lays it out (cimport only)
  |   --no-banner                   Print no banner: for scripts and tests
  |   -q, --quiet                   Print only the reports: no banner, no phase or status lines (scripts, tests)
  |   -h, --help                    Show the help of the command given (else adam's)
  |
  | TARGETS:
  |   x86_64-windows-gnu            (default)
  |   x86_64-linux-gnu
  |
  | EXAMPLES:
  |   adam build hello.adam
  |   adam build hello.adam -o bin
  |   adam build myproject
  |   adam check hello.adam
  |   adam init mygame exe
  |   adam pack mygame
  |   adam info mygame
  |   adam cimport zlib.cimport.toml
  |   adam dap
  |   adam lsp
  |   adam editor hello.adam
  |   adam help build
  |
  | Run 'adam help <command>' for one command's options and examples.
@@end
*/

module exe suite_cli_help;

begin
end.
